  {
    "id": "session-32-adore-is-up-in-flames_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 32 - Adore Is Up In Flames",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"32 - Adore Is Up In Smoke.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-32-1usboupVJ-3gF9-cKBbsZWHQp589ynVMJ.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1usboupVJ-3gF9-cKBbsZWHQp589ynVMJ\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"32 - Adore Is Up In Smoke.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1usboupVJ-3gF9-cKBbsZWHQp589ynVMJ/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "2",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-32-adore-is-up-in-flames_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party left Caelora determined to catch Pa’s caravan and learn the truth of the corruption Kaizo feared at the monastery of Adore. At the Rustlight campsite they encountered a wary band of Adore monks who admitted the monastery was dividing and advised them to stay away, while Affy received a chilling contract from the devil Ducrurith offering to free her soul in exchange for one of greater value. The next day they found Adore itself in flames and fought through waves of corrupted monks that poured from the smoke. When the last of the corrupted fell, Rueh’unar Heildove stepped into the clearing and declared that he was not their enemy.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "3",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-31-you-are-where-you-belong_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 31 - You Are Where You Belong",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"31 - You Are Where You Belong.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-31-1GSbtuIvwIgQ0Hv4QgeCXpXd5RWv96Fjw.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1GSbtuIvwIgQ0Hv4QgeCXpXd5RWv96Fjw\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"31 - You Are Where You Belong.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GSbtuIvwIgQ0Hv4QgeCXpXd5RWv96Fjw/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "4",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-31-you-are-where-you-belong_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party returned from Stygia to the Rulendor cellar in Caelora, determined to close the hellish portal and confront the aftermath of Urovil’s death. They severed the connection, learned an entire day had been lost, and split to pursue personal leads while Kaizo aided the monk Taelis, Relys learned her lantern stone held the spirit of her grandmother, and Kulv Farbreak pressed both Fungus and Affy to abandon Shotty Nell for the fey lord Selbranan. At noon Ridley, Cerul, and Relys told Lord Theravin the full truth of Hell; the lord accepted the account, declared the debt paid with gold and platinum, and released Ridley from all service. The next morning Fungus communed with Shotty Nell and confirmed that Affy was cursed by the devil Ducrurith, after which the party purchased an elven carriage and finally left Caelora behind.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "5",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-30-broken-oaths-and-the-fiend_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 30 - Broken Oaths & The Fiend",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"30 - Broken Oaths and the Fiend.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-30-15w3DYLR_oRNcAWBvRjIl0bNQrfppgS8p.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"15w3DYLR_oRNcAWBvRjIl0bNQrfppgS8p\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"30 - Broken Oaths and the Fiend.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/15w3DYLR_oRNcAWBvRjIl0bNQrfppgS8p/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "6",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-30-broken-oaths-and-the-fiend_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "Standing in the frozen hellscape of Stygia after pursuing Urovil through the portal, the party sought to defeat the guarding fiends, rescue the chained prisoner, confront Urovil, and escape back to the material plane. They battled an ice devil, its imps, and a bone devil in a fierce fight that saw Kaizo stun the devils repeatedly and Affy and Cerul deliver the killing blows before pressing on to Urovil’s chamber where a towering fiend patron appeared claim his soul, and offered the group safe passage with the body if they left his realm. A tense negotiation followed with blinding, stunning, and desperate escapes through the basin blood. The session ended with the party returning to the Rulendor cellar in Caelora, battered but alive with Urovil’s body in tow.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "7",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-29-into-hell_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 29 - Into Hell",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"29 - Into Hell.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-29-1J8bgXryjZDrDJuvy_U6HEK1ES-VQdmqB.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1J8bgXryjZDrDJuvy_U6HEK1ES-VQdmqB\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"29 - Into Hell.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J8bgXryjZDrDJuvy_U6HEK1ES-VQdmqB/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "8",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-29-into-hell_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party lingered in Caelora after their long journey, balancing personal quests and political threads while preparing to investigate the suspicious Rulendor cellar based on Nanise’s warnings. Evening meetings unfolded with Ridley and Eliyena navigating shifting alliances, Affy connecting with the enigmatic moontouched half-orc Kulv whose fey patron Selbranon offered cryptic aid tied to Fungus’s pact and Affy’s father, and Fungus and Cerul discovering Linden’s journal at an oddities shop that revealed Cerul’s glowing “last light of Pekanon” mark and the need to seek Maester Sylvandor in Basctdelm. At the Wayfarer’s Rest, Nanise revealed House Rulendor’s corruption and handed Ridley a key to the hidden cellar entrance, prompting a stealthy infiltration, before the group was pulled through a hellish portal into the frozen wastes of Stygia. There they faced biting cold, frozen horrors, and approaching fiends while scrambling to retreat, ending the session on a precarious cliffhanger as danger closed in from the balcony.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "9",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-28-caelora-has-issues_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 28 - Caelora has Issues",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"28 - Caelora has Issues.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-28-1ACgEGOFaPiYSlOg_zTmVn2M1dPaxIsRQ.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1ACgEGOFaPiYSlOg_zTmVn2M1dPaxIsRQ\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"28 - Caelora has Issues.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ACgEGOFaPiYSlOg_zTmVn2M1dPaxIsRQ/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "10",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-28-caelora-has-issues_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party continued to help Affy follow a lead in Basctdelm and help Ridley with business in Caelora.  At the Whisperpine campsite they encountered the moontouched half-orc adventurer Kulv Farbreak, who hinted at powers echoing Fungus’s own, while back at the fire a spirit of an elder druid from Iparos possessed Relys with a command to avenge her village. Upon reaching the terraced city,Urovil Rulendor greeted Ridley with news of an Airithel misfortune.  Cerul sensed something foul trailing from the towards House Rulendor and Kaizo’s earnest herb inquiries at Dawnpetal went sideways. Nanise Rulendor intercepted Ridley and abruptly relieved him of his duties.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "11",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-27-don-t-threaten-us_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 27 - Don't Threaten Us",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"27 - Don't Threaten Us.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-27-1YCNrVP02iiaABwgud83Q6w7Xq75btu2P.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1YCNrVP02iiaABwgud83Q6w7Xq75btu2P\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"27 - Don't Threaten Us.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1YCNrVP02iiaABwgud83Q6w7Xq75btu2P/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "12",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-27-don-t-threaten-us_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The caravan continued, but the morning calm shattered when an elvish wizard and a burly warrior thundered up demanding the prisoners’ release.  This sparked a wild battle that left the attackers dead but allowed Ridley’s long-sought robed elf to slip away by polymorphing into a rongri during the chaos. Later they captured Eliyena, a woman who insisted Ridley's prey, Heildove, was innocent of the crimes laid against him. The caravan reached the elven village Darafee by twilight and settled into the welcoming Cozy Toad, where storyteller Thallan Darego entertained the room with ominous tales of dark and hungry woods south of Murfield.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "13",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-26-to-caelora-and-beyond_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 26 - To Caelora and Beyond",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"26 - To Caelora and Beyond.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-26-1LHNkTKPhe8po714ZcVezICFvugx76Spu.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1LHNkTKPhe8po714ZcVezICFvugx76Spu\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"26 - To Caelora and Beyond.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1LHNkTKPhe8po714ZcVezICFvugx76Spu/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "14",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-26-to-caelora-and-beyond_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "They left Qal’dynn escorting three wagons to Shademoor:  one toting wine, one toting components and one toting prisoners.  Affy uncovered that one of the shackled prisoners was none other than Ridley’s long-sought assassination target. On the second day of travel, Fungus acquired a bulas and named it Trygg.  The group enjoyed an evening at the curious Ashbarrel Lodge where Fungus drank himself into a singing, dancing stupor. On the third day a blue-skinned Oni and three trolls attempted to collect a rather steep toll at a stone bridge. The party made short work of the monsters, taking the Oni’s rune-covered greatsword Trollsplitter and other treasures.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "15",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-25-to-qal-dynn_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 25 - To Qal'dynn",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"25 - To Qal'dynn.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-25-1RBImyCW5e4UEP9a54bmHlhZYbOj85Wtr.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1RBImyCW5e4UEP9a54bmHlhZYbOj85Wtr\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"25 - To Qal'dynn.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1RBImyCW5e4UEP9a54bmHlhZYbOj85Wtr/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "16",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-25-to-qal-dynn_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "Everyone exited the Blackstone Crucible with the abacus after testing the gate.  On the way to the Abbey, they met spectral giant Amag who warned Cerul of an unresolved scar beneath his birthplace in destroyed Pekanon. Kaizo continued to have difficulty meditating, hinting that Malgri'n was still an issue.  They took the Arcane Waypoint to Qal’dynn and met with Lorain Ormseer.  Gaining clues about Affy's father and the Promisory in Basctdelm, they agreed to pick up a job as guards for a few wagons that headed that way.  Ridley did have some unfinished matters with a clue he uncovered on his hunt for Heildove.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "17",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-24-into-the-shadowfell_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 24 - Into the Shadowfell",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"24 - Into the Shadowfell.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-24-1ZPfDzTJlyQe0IpkiRWL3NxQjtaTl8hYi.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1ZPfDzTJlyQe0IpkiRWL3NxQjtaTl8hYi\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"24 - Into the Shadowfell.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZPfDzTJlyQe0IpkiRWL3NxQjtaTl8hYi/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "18",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-24-into-the-shadowfell_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party set out to investigate and seal the dangerous rift between the material plane and the Shadowfell near Varenwood, and learn what they could of the ruined gnome village of Iparos. After receiving vital information from Zaedra Windfury of the Everdawn, they recovered faint magical remnants from the ruined settlement before stepping through the rift.  In the Shadowfell, waves of shadowy assailants and an avatar of Malgri'n assailed them, nearly claiming Fungus before the group rallied before defeated the avatar.  Tananan appeared and carried the Feywoven Glyphic away.  The party returned to the material plane and dispelled the rift’s anchoring magic.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "19",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-23-their-fates-tied_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 23 - Their Fates Tied",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"23 - Their Fates Tied.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-23-1GOTJVRHfXYHOjvlQTI5Rm7oDMA3tZXOG.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1GOTJVRHfXYHOjvlQTI5Rm7oDMA3tZXOG\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"23 - Their Fates Tied.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GOTJVRHfXYHOjvlQTI5Rm7oDMA3tZXOG/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "20",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-23-their-fates-tied_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party sought to understand the true purpose of the Blackstone Crucible and determine whether the powerful being bound within it should remain imprisoned. After encountering a Shadar-kai visitor investigating yugoloth activity and learning that Kael Vorduun had been bound as an example by Malgri’n, the party made a fateful oath to release him in exchange for binding another deemed worthy in the future. The session ended with the group stepping through the portal into Varenwood, realizing that Kaizo’s disrupted balance, Fungus’s patron’s imprisonment, and Relys’s ruined village were all tied together by the same force.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "21",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-22-the-blackstone-crucible_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 22 - The Blackstone Crucible",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"22 - The Blackstone Crucible.txt.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-22-1ZQXI5fp1n-gYSvFJygBowjTv7JyeN9Ls.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1ZQXI5fp1n-gYSvFJygBowjTv7JyeN9Ls\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"22 - The Blackstone Crucible.txt.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZQXI5fp1n-gYSvFJygBowjTv7JyeN9Ls/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "22",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-22-the-blackstone-crucible_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party entered a newly revealed black stone structure with the goal of understanding its purpose. Inside, they discovered it's name, the Blackstone Crucible, a vast and ancient construct devoted to the binding and containment of dangerous forces, guided by a rigid doctrine that framed imprisonment as mercy. Their exploration uncovered ritual chambers, indoctrination texts, and an encounter with extra-planar fiends. In the aftermath, the party discovered a mysterious gate calibrated to distant locations and encountered a strange counting entity that reported their presence to a figure named Varmuun.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "23",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-21-the-emerging-temple_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 21 - The Emerging Temple",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"21 - The Emerging Temple.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-21-1ZVIBOeA2zLV4WdUH5wIXmspRUeKZ6_H9.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1ZVIBOeA2zLV4WdUH5wIXmspRUeKZ6_H9\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"21 - The Emerging Temple.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ZVIBOeA2zLV4WdUH5wIXmspRUeKZ6_H9/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "24",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-21-the-emerging-temple_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party set out to investigate the deadly cave route near the Abbey, hoping to learn why no one returned and whether it connected to the wider threats they had been uncovering. Inside, they found signs of curse driven deaths and recovered evidence tying the site back to Dunduar and the strange forces already in motion. Their caution paid off when they defeated a corrupted stone giant guarding the path beyond the ravine. The session ended with a major revelation as the party emerged to find a massive black stone temple newly risen from the earth, its sealed doors marked with an ancient oath to a long forgotten power.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "25",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-20-restoring-the-abbey_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 20 - Restoring the Abbey",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"20 - Restoring the Abbey.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-20-1vqOnQxEhx80lDJS52nQQirVFI2H1TBnP.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1vqOnQxEhx80lDJS52nQQirVFI2H1TBnP\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"20 - Restoring the Abbey.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1vqOnQxEhx80lDJS52nQQirVFI2H1TBnP/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "26",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-20-restoring-the-abbey_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party worked to secure the Abbey now that its arcane waypoint was restored. They confronted a powerful infiltrator, the Parson, who revealed himself by turning allies to stone, but through coordinated effort and timely magic, the party defeated him and reversed the petrification. In the aftermath, they uncovered hidden vaults and sealed Underdark access beneath the Abbey, choosing restraint over greed to protect what had been entrusted to the order. The session closed with the Abbey finally safe, its people openly grateful, and the party recognized for having turned a looming collapse into a moment of renewed hope.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "27",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-19-ham-s-helping-hand_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 19 - Ham's Helping Hand",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
      "audioLinks": "[\n  {\n    \"label\": \"19 - Ham’s Helping Hand.mp3\",\n    \"url\": \"/media/session-audio/a-new-adventure/session-19-1neldkkkhq1UNx64WjtVdErqGYIazvwdw.mp3\",\n    \"sourceFileId\": \"1neldkkkhq1UNx64WjtVdErqGYIazvwdw\",\n    \"sourceFileName\": \"19 - Ham’s Helping Hand.mp3\",\n    \"sourceUrl\": \"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1neldkkkhq1UNx64WjtVdErqGYIazvwdw/view?usp=sharing\"\n  }\n]",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "28",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-19-ham-s-helping-hand_summary",
    "type": "text",
    "props": {
      "content": "The party pressed deeper beneath the Abbey with the goal of dismantling the Rel’Udomina cell. They exposed another operative group, confirmed that the conspiracy relied on ordinary members of the Abbey above ground, and learned the Rel’Udomina were structured into multiple Looms overseen by Archons. Pushing onward, they fought through possessed defenders and wraithlike entities guarding the waypoint chamber, breaking the possession and reactivating the portal. The session ended the moment the restored waypoint drew hostile attention, leaving the party face to face with a furious new threat just as help could finally reach the Abbey.",
      "col": "1",
      "row": "29",
      "colSpan": "1",
      "rowSpan": "1"
    }
  },
  {
    "id": "session-18-abbey-undercroft_title",
    "type": "header",
    "props": {
      "title": "Session 18 - Abbey Undercroft",
      "color": "gold",
      "size": "md",
